      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_164"
      ],
      "explanation": "Evaluate the quantity inside parentheses first. Since \\(2\\ne0\\), the zero-exponent rule gives \\(2^0=1\\), and \\(5^2=25\\). Therefore\n\\[\n2^0-1+5^2+0=1-1+25+0=25.\n\\]\nAn exponent of \\(-1\\) means taking the reciprocal of a nonzero number. Thus the requested value is\n\\[\n25^{-1}\\cdot5=\\frac1{25}\\cdot5\n=\\boxed{\\frac15},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
      "id": "evaluate-powers-and-reciprocal",
      "sourceRef": "amc/2015_AMC_12A_Q01#evaluate-powers-and-reciprocal",
      "title": "Evaluate the powers, then take the reciprocal"
    }
